    },
    {
        "content": "<p>actually, that might not even exist... hmmmm...</p>",
        "id": 597825755,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779797084
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the issue is that <code>v</code> may not be surjective</p>",
        "id": 597825817,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779797100
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Welcome to the world of non surjective valuations!</p>",
        "id": 597829566,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1779798154
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would using ValuativeRel change anything?</p>",
        "id": 597829941,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1779798254
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think so: <code>K</code> and <code>L</code> don't know anything about the value group of <code>v</code>, it can be absurdly big. The <em>image</em> of <code>v</code> is related to <code>K</code> of course but it seems unnatural to link the whole <code>Γ</code> to <code>ΓL</code>.</p>",
        "id": 597830523,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1779798425
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What you can probably define is a map <code>ValueGroup₀ v →*₀ ValueGroup₀ w</code>.</p>",
        "id": 597833316,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1779799164
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroup₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroup₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">restrict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroup₀</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">restrict₀_surjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">choose</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597833889,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1779799318
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The right object to work with is indeed <code>ValueGroup₀</code>, since you could always make <code>Γ</code> arbitrarily big. As Riccardo points out, while <code>v</code> might not be surjective, <code>v.restrict</code> always is (for <code>v</code> a valuation on a field).</p>",
        "id": 599339951,
        "sender_full_name": "María Inés de Frutos Fernández",
        "timestamp": 1780388261
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39953\">#39953</a></p>",
        "id": 599361532,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780394523
    }
]